package Vixen.TextureGraph.Shaders

import Vixen.Shaders.Core

// A stroke or a ribbon along a curve on the model — Patina #130 and #131.
//
// ## The table
//
// `points` is a table two rows high and one column per point of the polyline, written on the CPU from
// the curve the artist placed: row 0 is the point in the model's units and its pressure, row 1 its normal
// and how far along the path it is. `count` says how many columns are real. The kernel finds, for each
// texel, the nearest place on the polyline among the segments whose normal agrees with the texel's, and
// covers it by how far that is against the width there.
//
// ## Distance in space
//
// A texel's place on the model is the `position` bake, 0..1 over a box of its own, turned back into the
// model's units by `boxMin` and `boxSize` — the decal's reason: a distance in the bake's box is longer
// along a long side. ⚠ Distance in space is not distance along the surface, so a thin wall is near the
// curve on both of its sides. The normal is the guard: a segment whose normal is turned further than
// the angle whose cosine is `facing` from the texel's own is not that texel's to take.
//
// ## Stroke and ribbon
//
// A stroke (`ribbon` 0) shows the source as it lies on the atlas, through the path, so a constant colour
// or a material lands as a brush along a curve would leave it. A ribbon (`ribbon` 1) reads the source
// along the path instead: across the picture is how far along the path the nearest place is, over
// `period`, and down it is the side of the path the texel is on, the picture's top on the left as the
// path runs. ⚠ The picture wraps along the path and clamps across it, so it tiles end to end and never
// reads its other edge.
//
// ## Where a ribbon crosses itself
//
// A ribbon that loops back over itself lies on top of where it has already been, as a strip of tape
// would: the polyline is walked in order, each run of consecutive segments that reaches the texel is
// one pass over it, and each pass lays its picture over the passes before it. Within a pass the nearest
// segment wins, as it always did, so a bend is still one pass. ⚠ A segment the normal guard turns away
// neither ends a pass nor starts one: it is the far side of a wall, not the path leaving.
//
// ## Stamps along a stroke
//
// A stroke with `spacing` above zero is not one band but a row of round stamps, as a brush leaves one,
// their middles `spacing` apart along the path from its start (Patina #130). A texel takes the stamp
// nearest it among those its nearest segments reach, measured in the path's own frame: how far along,
// how far to the side, and what is left of the distance, which is off the surface or past the path's
// end. `jitter` moves each stamp by up to that share of the width to the side and of half the spacing
// along, by a hash of its number, so the same path jitters the same way on every host. ⚠ A ribbon
// reads its picture along the whole path and takes no stamps.
//
// With `shaped` 1 each stamp is a brush alpha rather than a disc: `alpha` is a table `alphaSide` texels
// square whose red is the alpha over the stamp's square, across it along the path and down it to the
// side, so a square alpha leaves square stamps that turn with the path. The width is the square's half
// side; what is left of the distance, off the surface, still has to be within it.
//
// ## A filled path
//
// With `filled` 1 the polyline is a loop, closed by the host, and what it encloses is covered as well as
// the band along it (Patina #130). Inside is decided in the loop's own plane, which the host gives as two
// unit vectors square to each other and to the loop's mean normal, `fillU` and `fillV`: the texel's place
// and every point are laid on that plane and an even-odd count of the edges crossed says whether the
// texel is within. A texel whose normal is turned further from the plane's than `facing` allows takes
// nothing inside, as the band's guard does. Past the loop the band falls away as a stroke's does, so the
// radius is the fill's soft edge.
//
// A loop is flattened on its plane, so on the plane alone another part behind or in front of the one the
// loop is drawn round, facing the same way, would be inside too (Patina #311). Height on the plane's
// normal is the second guard: a surface whose every face is within the angle of the plane's normal climbs
// no faster than the angle's tangent across it, so from the nearest place on the loop, at `d` on the
// plane, it can stand no further above or below the loop's height there than `d·tan(angle)`, and the
// radius. A texel further than that is another part seen through this one, and takes nothing inside. ⚠ A
// step steeper than the angle between the loop and a texel inside cuts the fill off at the step, as the
// angle says it should; a ribbon and stamps take no fill.
//
// ## The bound
//
// `reachMin` and `reachMax` are the polyline's box grown by its widest radius, and a texel outside it
// takes nothing without reading the table. Most of an atlas is outside any one path, so this is most of
// what keeps a path cheap.

shader SurfacePath {
    /// The picture: read through the path for a stroke, along it for a ribbon.
    var source: Texture2D

    /// The `position` bake: unsigned, 0..1 over its own box.
    var position: Texture2D

    /// The `world` bake: signed, `0.5 + 0.5·n`.
    var world: Texture2D

    /// The polyline: row 0 the points and their pressure, row 1 their normals and distance along the path.
    var points: Texture2D

    /// A brush alpha over a stamp's square, in red, `alphaSide` texels square. Read only while `shaped` is 1.
    var alpha: Texture2D

    /// How many points the table holds.
    var count: int = 0

    var boxMinX: float = 0f
    var boxMinY: float = 0f
    var boxMinZ: float = 0f
    var boxSizeX: float = 1f
    var boxSizeY: float = 1f
    var boxSizeZ: float = 1f

    var reachMinX: float = 0f
    var reachMinY: float = 0f
    var reachMinZ: float = 0f
    var reachMaxX: float = 0f
    var reachMaxY: float = 0f
    var reachMaxZ: float = 0f

    /// Half the path's width at full pressure, in the model's units.
    var radius: float = 0.01f

    /// How much of the width is at full strength before the edge falls away.
    var hardness: float = 0.5f

    /// The cosine of the widest angle a face may turn from the path's normal and still take it.
    var facing: float = 0.2674989f

    /// 1 reads the picture along the path; 0 reads it where the texel is on the atlas.
    var ribbon: int = 0

    /// How far along the path one repeat of a ribbon's picture runs, in the model's units. Zero keeps the
    /// picture's own shape at the path's width.
    var period: float = 0f

    /// How far apart a stroke's stamps are along the path, in the model's units. Zero is one unbroken band.
    var spacing: float = 0f

    /// How far each stamp moves at random: a share of the width to the side and of half the spacing along.
    var jitter: float = 0f

    /// 1 covers what the loop encloses as well as the band along it.
    var filled: int = 0

    /// The loop's plane: one unit vector across it.
    var fillUX: float = 1f
    var fillUY: float = 0f
    var fillUZ: float = 0f

    /// The loop's plane: the unit vector square to `fillU` across it.
    var fillVX: float = 0f
    var fillVY: float = 1f
    var fillVZ: float = 0f

    /// 1 shapes each stamp by `alpha`; 0 is a round stamp.
    var shaped: int = 0

    /// How many texels `alpha` has on a side.
    var alphaSide: int = 2

    [Format("rgba16f")] var target: RWTexture2D<float4>

    const val MaxPoints: int = 1024

    /// The most stamps one segment weighs for a texel: the host keeps the spacing at least a tenth of the width.
    const val MaxStamps: int = 32

    /// One pixel of the picture, wrapped across and clamped down.
    func Tap(x: int, y: int): float4 {
        val extent = source.GetDimensions(0)
        val wx = Math.Wrap(x, extent.x)

        return source.Load(int3(wx, clamp(y, 0, extent.y - 1), 0))
    }

    /// The picture at a place on it, 0..1 across and down, bilinearly.
    func At(u: float, v: float): float4 {
        val extent = source.GetDimensions(0)
        val px = u * float(extent.x) - 0.5f
        val py = v * float(extent.y) - 0.5f
        val x0 = int(floor(px))
        val y0 = int(floor(py))
        val tx = px - float(x0)
        val ty = py - float(y0)

        val top = lerp(Tap(x0, y0), Tap(x0 + 1, y0), float4(tx, tx, tx, tx))
        val bottom = lerp(Tap(x0, y0 + 1), Tap(x0 + 1, y0 + 1), float4(tx, tx, tx, tx))

        return lerp(top, bottom, float4(ty, ty, ty, ty))
    }

    /// One texel of a map that may be a different size from the image being written.
    func Read(map: Texture2D, coord: int2, size: int2): float4 {
        val extent = map.GetDimensions(0)
        val x = int(floor((float(coord.x) + 0.5f) * float(extent.x) / float(size.x)))
        val y = int(floor((float(coord.y) + 0.5f) * float(extent.y) / float(size.y)))

        return map.Load(int3(clamp(x, 0, extent.x - 1), clamp(y, 0, extent.y - 1), 0))
    }

    /// How much of a texel one place on the path covers, from its share of the width and its pressure.
    func Cover(share: float, pressure: float): float {
        val soft = max(1f - hardness, 0.000001f)

        return saturate((1f - share) / soft) * saturate(pressure)
    }

    /// One texel of the alpha, nothing outside it.
    func AlphaTap(x: int, y: int): float {
        if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= alphaSide || y >= alphaSide) {
            return 0f
        }

        return alpha.Load(int3(x, y, 0)).x
    }

    /// The alpha at a place on a stamp, -1..1 along the path and to its side, bilinearly; nothing past its square.
    func Shape(along: float, side: float): float {
        val px = (along * 0.5f + 0.5f) * float(alphaSide) - 0.5f
        val py = (side * 0.5f + 0.5f) * float(alphaSide) - 0.5f
        val x0 = int(floor(px))
        val y0 = int(floor(py))
        val tx = px - float(x0)
        val ty = py - float(y0)
        val top = lerp(AlphaTap(x0, y0), AlphaTap(x0 + 1, y0), tx)
        val bottom = lerp(AlphaTap(x0, y0 + 1), AlphaTap(x0 + 1, y0 + 1), tx)

        return lerp(top, bottom, ty)
    }

    /// How much the nearest of a stroke's stamps covers a texel, from where the texel is in the path's frame: `at`
    /// along the path, `side` across it, `rest` the square of the distance left over, `length` the path's whole.
    func Stamped(at: float, side: float, rest: float, wide: float, pressure: float, length: float): float {
        val drift = jitter * spacing * 0.5f
        val first = max(int(floor((at - wide - drift) / spacing)), 0)
        val last = min(int(ceil((at + wide + drift) / spacing)), int(floor(length / spacing)))
        var most = 0f

        for (step in 0 .. MaxStamps - 1) {
            val k = first + step

            if (k > last) {
                break
            }

            val centre = float(k) * spacing + drift * Random.Signed(Random.Hash2(uint(k), 1u))
            val beside = jitter * wide * Random.Signed(Random.Hash2(uint(k), 2u))
            val da = at - centre
            val ds = side - beside
            val share = sqrt(da * da + ds * ds + rest) / wide
            val shapedCover = rest < wide * wide ? Shape(da / wide, ds / wide) * saturate(pressure) : 0f

            most = max(most, shaped != 0 ? shapedCover : Cover(share, pressure))
        }

        return most
    }

    /// The ribbon's picture where one pass reaches a texel.
    func Laid(along: float, side: float, across: float): float4 {
        val extent = source.GetDimensions(0)
        val run = period > 0f ? period : 2f * across * float(extent.x) / float(max(extent.y, 1))

        return At(along / max(run, 0.000001f), 0.5f - side * 0.5f)
    }

    /// Whether a place is within the loop, laid on its plane, by an even-odd count of the edges it crosses, and
    /// no higher or lower than a surface within the angle could climb to from the nearest place on the loop.
    func Enclosed(p: float3, texelNormal: float3): bool {
        val u = float3(fillUX, fillUY, fillUZ)
        val v = float3(fillVX, fillVY, fillVZ)
        val w = cross(u, v)

        if (dot(w, texelNormal) < facing) {
            return false
        }

        val pu = dot(p, u)
        val pv = dot(p, v)
        var crossings = 0

        // The nearest place on the loop, on the plane: how far it is, squared, and the loop's height there.
        var nearest = 1e30f
        var nearestHeight = 0f

        for (i in 0 .. MaxPoints - 1) {
            if (i + 1 >= count) {
                break
            }

            val a = points.Load(int3(i, 0, 0))
            val b = points.Load(int3(i + 1, 0, 0))
            val au = dot(float3(a.x, a.y, a.z), u)
            val av = dot(float3(a.x, a.y, a.z), v)
            val bu = dot(float3(b.x, b.y, b.z), u)
            val bv = dot(float3(b.x, b.y, b.z), v)

            if ((av > pv && bv <= pv) || (bv > pv && av <= pv)) {
                val meets = au + (pv - av) / (bv - av) * (bu - au)

                if (pu < meets) {
                    crossings = crossings + 1
                }
            }

            val eu = bu - au
            val ev = bv - av
            val reach = eu * eu + ev * ev
            val t = reach > 0f ? saturate(((pu - au) * eu + (pv - av) * ev) / reach) : 0f
            val du = pu - (au + eu * t)
            val dv = pv - (av + ev * t)
            val apart = du * du + dv * dv

            if (apart < nearest) {
                nearest = apart
                nearestHeight = lerp(dot(float3(a.x, a.y, a.z), w), dot(float3(b.x, b.y, b.z), w), t)
            }
        }

        if (crossings % 2 == 0) {
            return false
        }

        // How fast a surface within the angle may climb: the angle's tangent, unbounded at a right angle or more.
        val slope = facing > 0.000001f ? sqrt(max(1f - facing * facing, 0f)) / facing : 1e30f

        return abs(dot(p, w) - nearestHeight) <= sqrt(nearest) * slope + radius
    }

    /// One pass laid over what the passes before it laid, premultiplied.
    func Over(under: float4, along: float, side: float, across: float, share: float, pressure: float): float4 {
        val picture = Laid(along, side, across)
        val a = picture.w * Cover(share, pressure)
        val keep = 1f - a

        return float4(picture.x * a + under.x * keep, picture.y * a + under.y * keep, picture.z * a + under.z * keep, a + under.w * keep)
    }

    [ComputeShader(8, 8, 1)]
    func Main([Semantic("SV_DispatchThreadID")] id: uint3) {
        val coord = int2(int(id.x), int(id.y))
        val size = target.GetDimensions()

        if (coord.x >= size.x || coord.y >= size.y) {
            return
        }

        val nothing = float4(0f, 0f, 0f, 0f)
        val place = Read(position, coord, size)
        val p = float3(boxMinX + place.x * boxSizeX, boxMinY + place.y * boxSizeY, boxMinZ + place.z * boxSizeZ)

        if (count < 1 || p.x < reachMinX || p.y < reachMinY || p.z < reachMinZ || p.x > reachMaxX || p.y > reachMaxY || p.z > reachMaxZ) {
            target.Store(coord, nothing)

            return
        }

        val encoded = Read(world, coord, size)
        val n = float3(encoded.x * 2f - 1f, encoded.y * 2f - 1f, encoded.z * 2f - 1f)
        val reach = sqrt(dot(n, n))

        if (reach <= 0.000001f) {
            target.Store(coord, nothing)

            return
        }

        val texelNormal = n / reach

        // The nearest place, as a share of its own width: below one is covered.
        var best = 2f
        var strength = 0f

        // A stroke in stamps: the most any stamp covers, and the path's whole length, which the last stamp is within.
        val stamps = ribbon == 0 && filled == 0 && spacing > 0f
        val total = stamps ? points.Load(int3(count - 1, 1, 0)).w : 0f
        var stamped = 0f

        // A ribbon's passes: the one being walked, and everything the finished ones laid, premultiplied.
        var laid = float4(0f, 0f, 0f, 0f)
        var inPass = 0
        var passBest = 2f
        var passAlong = 0f
        var passSide = 0f
        var passStrength = 0f
        var passAcross = 0f

        for (i in 0 .. MaxPoints - 1) {
            if (i >= count) {
                break
            }

            // A table of one point is a dot: the segment from it to itself.
            val j = min(i + 1, count - 1)

            if (i > 0 && j == i) {
                break
            }

            val a = points.Load(int3(i, 0, 0))
            val b = points.Load(int3(j, 0, 0))
            val na = points.Load(int3(i, 1, 0))
            val nb = points.Load(int3(j, 1, 0))

            val from = float3(a.x, a.y, a.z)
            val span = float3(b.x, b.y, b.z) - from
            val length = dot(span, span)
            val t = length > 0f ? saturate(dot(p - from, span) / length) : 0f
            val on = from + span * t
            val pathNormal = float3(na.x, na.y, na.z) * (1f - t) + float3(nb.x, nb.y, nb.z) * t
            val normalReach = sqrt(dot(pathNormal, pathNormal))

            if (normalReach <= 0.000001f || dot(pathNormal, texelNormal) / normalReach < facing) {
                continue
            }

            val pressure = a.w * (1f - t) + b.w * t
            val wide = max(radius * pressure, 0.000001f)
            val offset = p - on
            val share = sqrt(dot(offset, offset)) / wide

            // The side the texel is on, with the path running along `span` over a surface facing `pathNormal`.
            val leftward = cross(pathNormal / normalReach, length > 0f ? span / sqrt(length) : float3(0f, 0f, 0f))
            val here = na.w * (1f - t) + nb.w * t
            val sideHere = dot(offset, leftward) / wide

            if (share < best) {
                best = share
                strength = pressure
            }

            if (stamps && share < 1f + jitter) {
                val direction = length > 0f ? span / sqrt(length) : float3(0f, 0f, 0f)
                val beyond = dot(offset, direction)
                val side = dot(offset, leftward)
                val rest = max(dot(offset, offset) - side * side - beyond * beyond, 0f)

                stamped = max(stamped, Stamped(here + beyond, side, rest, wide, pressure, total))
            }

            if (share < 1f) {
                if (inPass == 0 || share < passBest) {
                    passBest = share
                    passAlong = here
                    passSide = sideHere
                    passStrength = pressure
                    passAcross = wide
                }

                inPass = 1
            } else if (inPass != 0) {
                laid = Over(laid, passAlong, passSide, passAcross, passBest, passStrength)
                inPass = 0
            }
        }

        if (inPass != 0) {
            laid = Over(laid, passAlong, passSide, passAcross, passBest, passStrength)
        }

        if (stamps) {
            val shown = At((float(coord.x) + 0.5f) / float(size.x), (float(coord.y) + 0.5f) / float(size.y))

            target.Store(coord, float4(shown.x, shown.y, shown.z, shown.w * stamped))

            return
        }

        if (filled != 0 && Enclosed(p, texelNormal)) {
            val within = At((float(coord.x) + 0.5f) / float(size.x), (float(coord.y) + 0.5f) / float(size.y))

            target.Store(coord, within)

            return
        }

        if (best >= 1f) {
            target.Store(coord, nothing)

            return
        }

        if (ribbon != 0) {
            val alpha = max(laid.w, 0.000001f)

            target.Store(coord, float4(laid.x / alpha, laid.y / alpha, laid.z / alpha, laid.w))

            return
        }

        val picture = At((float(coord.x) + 0.5f) / float(size.x), (float(coord.y) + 0.5f) / float(size.y))

        target.Store(coord, float4(picture.x, picture.y, picture.z, picture.w * Cover(best, strength)))
    }
}
